The year is 3017. The world is changed. Magistrates rule now and they have strict rules.
Every baby born mist have its soul taken and stored in liquid form.
The children will learn to read, write and any necessary skills to help in society.
At the age of 18 a job will be appointed to them according their best skillset in school.
As these, gorwn ups now, complete tasks in their field a little bit of their soul is given back to them before the final judgment of God for Eternal Life or not.
Here we meet Aen. He's 18 years old and the job of cleric has been assigned to him.
A cleric is a potential Magistrate which means his role is seriously important. He's also a good candidate for Eternal Life.
He has to attend to the needs of the people, come up with new tech and most of all, help other magistrates in their decisions and, most important of all, keep secrets. Many secrets.
As he progresses through the cleric ranks, by doing exceptional work, he reaches the rank of Archbishop. Then his first initiation for the rank of Magistrate happens.
Aen takes the initiation right but suddenly a large explosion is heard from outside. Every Magistrate runs outside the room to see what's happening. 
With half his soul recovered Aen sees the Holy Bible on the table and curiosity takes the better of him.
He opens it and goes straight to the end. There he reads:
"Every life, every soul ever conceived is preordained by Us, the Archmagistrates. We define what the world and life is."
Shocked his leaves the Bible back at its place.
He knows he has to keep it a secret but he starts having doubts about this whole society he lives in.
He needs answers and he's stubborn enough to find them.
He goes to his mentor and makes half a joke that eveyrything is predsgned by the Magistrates to see his reaction.
His mentor laughs and tells him he's got great imagination.
As he walks back home the Church Police tries to stop him.
He escapes and goes as far from the city as possible.
Suddenly he gets a call from his sister, He picks up and his mentor tells him if he wants to see her alive again he has to come back.
He does and his mentor tells him the Magistrates are indeed the ones behind everything.
When Aen asks why they have designed sucha a cruel world, when they could have turned everyrone kind, his mentor tells him that progress needs time and testing.
They have a plan and they do control everything but they can never know how things will really play out unless they observe progress slowly.
And he tells him one more thing. They are afraid of the universe. Noone knows what might exist out there so they have an ultimate plan.
Divide the world and their Master Plan in smaller Plans that will be alive and a reincarnation of the souls the Magistrates have been gathering. The plans will be called Histories and offer Divine insight as to what the best course of action is based n current evidence.
They will be overseers of everything and they will intervene only when something is going really wrong.
Aen listens carefully and asks his mentor what would happen if an alien invasion happened today.
His mentor is honest and tells him, everyone would most probably die and all of history would be in vain.
Aen agrees that alive Plans that can transcend species then is the best idea. He has an objection though, the Plans should not be born out of trapped Souls but of free ones.
His mentor calls him unwise and tells him he needs more time as a Magistrate to understand their decisions.
Aen indeed waits and after many years pass, Magistrates are immortal after all, they all agree that the time has come to free humanity's Soul and implement their Histories idea based on these free souls.
